---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Process | Griffith Creative"
  description="How an engagement with Griffith Creative runs: a call, a written scope, the build, and what happens after launch."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container-site">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-7">Process</p>
      <h1 class="h1 mb-7">How we work.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The same shape for a single site and a company-wide rebuild.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site">
      <div class="stacked">
      <h2 class="h2">Scope</h2>
      <p class="para">
        It starts with a fifteen-minute call. If we are the right fit, you get a written scope with a fixed price and a timeline: what is included, what is not, how many revision rounds, and how we respond. Nothing starts until it is signed.
      </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">Build</h2>
      <p class="para">
        A working preview inside the first two weeks, reviewed in the browser. Revisions are part of the scope, and scope changes are priced and agreed in writing before they start. Before launch we measure performance, accessibility, and search structure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site">
      <p class="statement">
        After launch, every account is handed over in your name. <a href="/care" class="underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent">Care Plan</a> covers sites, ongoing management covers enterprise, and either side can end an ongoing plan with thirty days notice. Everything stays yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="container-site">
      <h2 class="h2-close mb-8">Start with a call.</h2>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
